                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Public health and the environment still matter. Strong efficiency rules cut pollution, protect kids, and save families money at the pump. Weakening them locks Americans into higher fuel costs and more dependence on foreign oil. That is not conservative and it is not smart.\n\nEV prices are falling and families save on maintenance over the life of the car. People deserve choices that lower their costs, not decisions that tie them to outdated technology.",
