                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 36,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Congress has only this week and next in Washington, and now Deputy Speaker Mike Johnson and House Republicans are scrambling at the very last minute to piece something together on health care. They still don\u2019t have an agreement to save the ACA tax credits that expire at the end of the year. Not exactly inspiring leadership.\n\nThis is nothing more than an eleventh-hour attempt to pretend they have \u201cconcepts of a plan\u201d after spending a decade without one. In that time they took more than 70 swings at dismantling the ACA and produced nothing that actually helps families.\n\nWhat they have done is push a false claim that the ACA is somehow riddled with fraud. Independent fact checkers have found little evidence. At best, House Republican leaders are twisting the data to sell the cuts tucked into their Big Ugly Bill.\n\nMeanwhile, some Senate Republicans, and even a few House Republicans who broke with their leadership, have at least put ideas on the table that are worth a real bipartisan conversation. But none of that matters if Johnson and his team keep flailing. Their lack of leadership and last-minute scramble now risks leaving millions of Americans high and dry when premiums spike next year.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
